## JavaScript in the UI

Grape's windows are web pages that Vite bundles at build time. Two pieces of third-party code end up in them:

- [@tauri-apps/api 2.12.1](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tauri-apps/api/v/2.12.1) (Apache-2.0 OR MIT; Grape takes MIT): the calls that let the pages talk to Grape and listen for its events.
- [Vite 8.3.3](https://www.npmjs.com/package/vite/v/8.3.3) (MIT): the small module preload polyfill at the top of the pages' scripts.

The UI has no other runtime dependencies, and the build adds no other helpers. This section is written by hand: check it again when `apps/desktop/ui/package.json` or Vite changes.

